      framework_description: "Human behavior encompasses the full range of actions and reactions exhibited by individuals in response to internal and external stimuli. It is shaped by a complex interplay of biological, psychological, and social factors.\n.1. Biological Foundations\nBehavior is rooted in the brain's neural activity. The nervous system, hormones, and genetics all play crucial roles in determining how we act. The brain's plasticity allows behavior to change through experience.\n.2. Psychological Influences\nMental processes such as perception, memory, emotion, and motivation drive behavior. Cognitive psychology examines how information processing leads to actions, while psychodynamic approaches explore unconscious influences.\n.3. Social Context\nBehavior does not occur in a vacuum. Social norms, cultural expectations, relationships, and group dynamics constantly shape and modify individual behavior. The social environment can dramatically alter how a person acts.",
